- Fully rewrote bundled plugins to run in isolates
- Added timeouts to all plugin calls
- Bundled plugin calls now record their network requests (not yet included in bug reports)
- Plugins now report isolate setup errors instead of hanging at init, and fail at once on uncaught async errors

- Added `unavailableFields` so plugins can list fields they cannot scrape
- Replaced `scrapeFailMessage` with `scrapeFailException`
- Plugins now receive HTTP response headers through a new `requestHttp` function
- Plugin email and bug report URLs are now optional
- Reserved the bundled plugins namespace
- Plugin update links now require HTTPS, and non-HTTPS icon links trigger a warning
- Added testing for third-party plugins and initial third-party plugin docs

- Made all onboarding screens scrollable, with bottom buttons always visible
- Reduced the default padding in video lists
- Preview images now preserve aspect ratio (instead of being stretched)
- Comment sections now only render when they are shown
- Plugin descriptions now show the issue tracker URL
- The update failure message now links to the download page

- All history dates are now stored as integers
- Fields listed in `unavailableFields` are no longer stored in history

- Fixed both xhamster and pornhub bundled plugins

- Fixed the update check always reporting a new version
- Fixed the bug report screen opening on rendering errors in release mode
- Fixed a null exception when bug reports are not submitted
- Fixed the video player not being centered on square displays
- Fixed the wrong background color in fullscreen mode
- Fixed `RangeError` when a video has exactly one quality
- Fixed the "no search providers enabled" warning showing when providers were enabled

- Added a separate x86_64 testing artifact to releases
- Updated the Android toolchain (Gradle 9.5.0, AGP 9.3.1, Kotlin 2.4.20)

**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/Hedon-Haven/Hedon-Haven/compare/v0.6.7...v0.6.8
